  "notes": [
    "One file for the JS importer (js/cost_basis_fop_import.js, handed this document by the page) and the server (cost_basis_fop_statement.py). Changing a status or an alias is a code change, never a runtime switch.",
    "A key is format/section/asset/event. The asset may carry a qualifier (FOP.cash_settled) for rows whose format is ordinary but whose product is outside the first release.",
    "The aliases come from the plan and from the stock importer's verified Activity and Flex exports. No FOP or FUT row has a de-identified real sample yet, so every economic key stays synthetic_only (plan §9.7). The layouts the synthetic fixtures assume are listed in tests/fixtures/cost_basis_fop/statements/README.md.",
    "Rows of the instrument and open-position sections are evidence (contract terms, delivery months, bindings, quantity proof), never events, so as rows they are out_of_scope. A Flex export is read as one flat Trades table.",
    "discriminators names the Trades rows the importer knows: an order, its executions, and detail rows (closed lots) that repeat a trade. A row with any other DataDiscriminator is an unread economic row and blocks its batch (plan §9.4).",
    "orderId links an order-level row to its executions across files; without it, rows of different granularity are never assumed to be the same fill."
  ],
  "statusDefinitions": {
    "real_verified": "Accepted from a de-identified real statement: needs at least one evidence entry of kind deidentified_real with verifiedOn and mappingVersion. Only these keys may be written.",
    "synthetic_only": "No real-statement acceptance. Preview only; a matching manual event may claim the row (plan §9.7). A synthetic evidence entry, when present, records that the synthetic fixture passed; it never makes the key writable.",
    "out_of_scope": "Recognised and deliberately not imported (daily settlement and cash sections, plan §6.3; evidence sections). Neither blocks nor writes.",
    "unsupported": "A recognised economic row the first release does not support (plan §1.2). Blocks its batch and cannot be claimed by a manual event."
  },
